# `list[i] == 100.5` in a loop over what is written number[]. Link has proven of the elements fractions, and objects of which nothing is known: that says nothing, so the guess at an element of numbers opens.
# The read out of Int32 storage asks nothing of the number that it finds, so it says int32 whatever Link has proven of the list: the way behind its two tests goes on with an int32. It used to end in Unreachable on Link's word alone.
# Double storage is asked in its turn, and its read gives any number: what may be a fraction without bounds is held to nothing narrower.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: [[int32]]: boolean @Boolean = HasArrayStorage [[list]] arrayStorage=Int32
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[int32]] -> taken [[present]](), notTaken [[other]]()
# CHECK: [[other]]() isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: [[double]]: boolean @Boolean = HasArrayStorage [[list]] arrayStorage=Double
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[double]] ->
# CHECK: [[present]]() isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: [[found]]: boolean @Boolean = IsElementPresent [[list]], {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[found]] -> taken [[something]](),
# CHECK: [[something]]() isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: : i32 @Int32 = GetArrayElement [[list]], {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# CHECK: : number @Double = GetArrayElement [[list]], {{*}}arrayStorage=Double
# -- source: a-read-out-of-int32-storage-goes-on-with-an-int32-whatever-is-proven-of-the-list-from-source.ts
